  "details": "While this can be done with a ton of Animation Controller Parameters, layers, and blendtrees, it would be incredibly useful for avatar optimization if it was built into VrC.\n\nEssentially, the idea is that in the Avatar Parameters inspector, you can assign a Binary Resolution to Ints and Floats. So instead of all floats/ints using 8 parameter slots for a 256 resolution, an avatar creator could adjust the parameter to for example only use 3 parameter slots for a resolution of 8. Thus saving a lot of parameter space that would be wasted.\n\nIn addition to Binary Resolution, floats could have the option of automatic smoothing, where the value of the float will interpolate from the 2nd latest value on other clients to the latest value in between packages. Making it slightly more delayed, but smooth and accurate. Or a possible predictive smoothing option where a float will consider its previous values to interpolate to a predicted value until the next expected package.",
